  "final_message": "The key written to the audit log is `AUD-ORDER-7781`. I confirmed this by running the code.\n\nHow it gets there:\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `_format_key` builds the key as `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n3. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, so the key becomes `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe `key = [REDACTED:SECRET]'t see it directly. I ran `write_audit('order','7781')` instead: the key it wrote has 14 characters, and its only non-alphanumeric characters are two hyphens, which matches `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` builds a similar-looking `MET-...` key, but it writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
